# Optional: route exchange-rate lookups through the app's own backend.
#
# Leave this UNSET and the app still works: `services/rateProviders.ts` calls
# several independent public rate providers and fails over between them, so no
# single host being blocked, rate-limited or retired can stop currency
# conversion.
#
# Set it to additionally take the browser out of the rate path, which is the
# only configuration that cannot be defeated by a third-party CORS policy or a
# content blocker.
#
# 1) Deploy the bundled proxy (needs Supabase CLI + project access):
#      supabase functions deploy exchange-rates
#
# 2) Apply supabase/migrations/0004_rate_proxy.sql (optional; the client can call
#    the function over HTTP without it, but the RPC is the path that needs no
#    custom headers).
#
# 3) Set the URL below and restart the bundler. No trailing slash.
EXPO_PUBLIC_EXCHANGE_RATE_PROXY_URL=
